WEBVTT

00:00.805 --> 00:04.035
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.135 --> 00:07.404
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.438 --> 00:10.974
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.008 --> 00:13.977
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:14.011 --> 00:17.480
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:17.515 --> 00:20.817
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.852 --> 00:22.385
♪ All the things that make us

00:22.420 --> 00:23.787
♪ Laugh and cry

00:23.821 --> 00:25.821
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.432 --> 00:37.967
Hey, thanks for helping me pick
out a new computer, you guys.

00:38.001 --> 00:39.268
Oh, no problem,
Quagmire.

00:39.303 --> 00:40.970
God, this place is
always so crowded.

00:41.004 --> 00:42.572
We gotta find someone
who works here.

00:42.606 --> 00:43.840
Can I help you, sir?

00:43.874 --> 00:46.342
Sorry, all I got
is a quarter, pal.

00:46.377 --> 00:47.977
Oh, excuse me, sir.

00:48.011 --> 00:49.979
My buddy here is
looking for a computer.

00:50.013 --> 00:51.914
I would like to elect you
president.

00:53.984 --> 00:55.118
What are you doing?

00:55.152 --> 00:57.120
You gonna get a new phone
while we're here?

00:57.154 --> 00:58.654
Maybe. But I gotta see
which one

00:58.689 --> 01:01.257
I wanna take in and out of
my pocket every 30 seconds

01:01.291 --> 01:02.492
for the next six years.

01:02.526 --> 01:03.766
What do you think,
Peter? Peter?

01:03.794 --> 01:06.929
I touched a iPhone headphone.

01:08.799 --> 01:10.933
You know what?
I think I'm gonna go with this one.

01:10.968 --> 01:13.102
Guy said it's the newest version.
Just came out this week.

01:13.137 --> 01:14.103
Ah, good call,
Quagmire.

01:14.138 --> 01:15.505
You're gonna be like
the first guy

01:15.539 --> 01:17.106
in the neighborhood
to own a Model T.

01:19.476 --> 01:21.077
See ya, suckers!

01:21.111 --> 01:24.847
I'll be there an hour after you
with throw-up all over my legs!

01:28.352 --> 01:30.219
Are you getting excited
for Halloween, Stewie?

01:30.254 --> 01:32.121
You know, we'll have
to start thinking

01:32.156 --> 01:33.489
about your costume soon.

01:33.524 --> 01:34.957
All right, but let's make sure

01:34.992 --> 01:36.692
we don't cover up this,
all right?

01:36.727 --> 01:38.628
It's what puts candy in the bag.

01:38.662 --> 01:40.430
Oh, look, Chris,
here's your costume

01:40.464 --> 01:42.465
from the year you went
as a condom.

01:42.499 --> 01:45.134
What the hell are you
supposed to be?

01:45.169 --> 01:48.337
Oh, Stewie, look!

01:48.372 --> 01:50.773
It's your very
first teddy bear!

01:52.209 --> 01:54.177
Oscar?

01:54.211 --> 01:56.012
Wow, I remember
that bear.

01:56.046 --> 01:57.980
That's the one Grandma
and Grandpa brought Stewie

01:58.015 --> 01:59.882
when he was still
in the hospital.

01:59.917 --> 02:01.717
Oh, and here's the card
they sent me.

02:01.752 --> 02:06.422
"Three kids on $40,000?
Have fun with your crap life."

02:06.457 --> 02:08.257
I guess he got tucked
away up here.

02:08.292 --> 02:09.826
You want him back,
sweetie?

02:13.397 --> 02:14.430
What, this old thing?

02:14.465 --> 02:15.698
No, no, thank you.
I've grown.

02:15.732 --> 02:16.732
I've changed.

02:16.767 --> 02:18.201
You sure you
don't want him?

02:18.235 --> 02:19.368
I said no, okay?

02:19.403 --> 02:20.736
Don't you have
a wedding dress

02:20.771 --> 02:22.738
to try halfway on
and then cry about?

02:27.578 --> 02:29.345
Hello? Oh, hey, Quagmire.
What's up?

02:29.379 --> 02:31.681
Hey, Peter, I need
some help with my computer.

02:31.715 --> 02:32.949
I can't find my photos.

02:32.983 --> 02:34.217
Did you look
under "Photos"?

02:34.251 --> 02:35.351
What is that?

02:35.385 --> 02:36.652
It's a folder
called "Photos."

02:36.687 --> 02:37.920
Yeah, I-I don't have that.

02:37.955 --> 02:39.956
I just have 40 folders
all called "New Folder."

02:39.990 --> 02:41.991
Okay. You know what?
Click on your hard drive.

02:42.025 --> 02:43.593
Okay, now-now the arrow
on the screen,

02:43.627 --> 02:44.894
that's me, right?

02:44.928 --> 02:46.762
Yeah, yeah, that's you.
Okay, now-now just...

02:46.797 --> 02:48.798
Whoa-whoa-whoa!
There's a calculator on this thing?!

02:48.832 --> 02:51.000
Listen, Quagmire,
what are you trying to do?

02:51.034 --> 02:51.929
I just wanna put pictures
of my cat

02:51.930 --> 02:53.355
on everyone's
Internet computer.

02:53.356 --> 02:54.556
Like, how do I do that?

02:54.938 --> 02:56.772
Okay, wait. There's an agreement
that just popped up.

02:56.807 --> 02:58.441
Hang on. L-Let me read
the whole thing.

02:58.475 --> 02:59.642
Just hit "Accept."

02:59.676 --> 03:01.477
Well, that seems a little foolhardy,
doesn't it, Peter?

03:01.512 --> 03:03.145
Look, do we have
to do this now?

03:03.180 --> 03:04.146
I'm watching something.

03:04.181 --> 03:05.147
I know. I'm sorry.

03:05.182 --> 03:06.516
I-I'm just nervous
that somebody else

03:06.550 --> 03:08.651
is gonna get pictures
of their cat on the Internet first,

03:08.685 --> 03:10.620
and then I'll always be known
as the second guy

03:10.654 --> 03:12.488
to get pictures of his cat
on the Internet.

03:12.523 --> 03:14.390
Quagmire, I don't know
how to tell you this,

03:14.424 --> 03:15.925
but there's already
cats on the Internet.

03:15.959 --> 03:17.460
Wait, it's-it's giving me
that pinwheel thing.

03:17.494 --> 03:20.263
It-It's frozen. Oh, my God,
oh, my God, it crashed!

03:20.297 --> 03:21.731
The whole thing
just crashed!

03:21.765 --> 03:22.832
Geez, Quagmire,
calm down.

03:22.866 --> 03:23.933
We'll figure it out.

03:23.967 --> 03:25.468
No, Peter,
the whole thing's fried!

03:25.502 --> 03:26.569
I can't even...!

03:26.603 --> 03:28.271
Ah! damn it!
What the hell?!

03:28.305 --> 03:30.139
Hey, you clicked "Accept."

03:33.443 --> 03:35.244
Hey, what's going on?

03:35.279 --> 03:36.746
You doing some
reading there?

03:36.780 --> 03:38.548
Yes, well, you know
I turn to poetry

03:38.582 --> 03:40.449
when matters of the heart
weigh heavily on me.

03:40.484 --> 03:42.184
"If you're happy
and you know it,

03:42.219 --> 03:45.655
"then your face will
surely show it.

03:45.689 --> 03:47.723
"If you're happy
and you know it,

03:47.758 --> 03:49.325
"clap your hands.

03:49.359 --> 03:50.326
Anonymous."

03:50.360 --> 03:51.627
Wait-- matters
of the heart?

03:51.662 --> 03:53.029
What are you
talking about?

03:53.063 --> 03:55.731
Well, Lois found my old teddy
bear, Oscar, in the attic.

03:55.766 --> 03:57.967
And I'm just not sure how
to handle it,

03:58.001 --> 03:59.602
what with Rupert and all.

03:59.636 --> 04:01.203
Who cares?
Just play with them both.

04:01.238 --> 04:02.438
I can't do that!

04:02.472 --> 04:04.073
Oh, it would be
so awkward!

04:04.107 --> 04:05.441
Um... okay.

04:05.475 --> 04:06.776
Oscar was my...

04:06.810 --> 04:08.511
well, he was my first,
you know.

04:08.545 --> 04:09.946
And that's always exciting.

04:09.980 --> 04:12.081
But-but I've been
with Rupert for so long now.

04:12.115 --> 04:13.082
Uh-huh.

04:13.116 --> 04:14.617
Most of our finances
are intertwined.

04:14.651 --> 04:16.052
We've built
a life together.

04:16.086 --> 04:17.887
On the other hand,
Oscar...

04:17.921 --> 04:20.189
Oscar's the only one who can
really make me laugh.

04:20.223 --> 04:23.693
I hate to say it, but I'm mostly
with Rupert because of his insurance.

04:23.727 --> 04:25.328
Stewie, I think you're
overthinking this.

04:25.362 --> 04:26.963
No, you're right.
You're right, Brian.

04:26.997 --> 04:28.030
I'm with Rupert now.

04:28.065 --> 04:29.765
I just need
to forget Oscar.

04:29.800 --> 04:32.134
No matter how intense
our relationship was.

04:36.006 --> 04:37.940
That's amazing.

04:37.975 --> 04:39.909
It's like you took
all the colors that exist

04:39.943 --> 04:43.145
and said, ",
here's a new one."

04:47.584 --> 04:48.918
Hi, can I help you?

04:48.952 --> 04:49.919
Well, that depends.

04:49.953 --> 04:51.621
Do you know how
to fix pieces of junk?!

04:51.655 --> 04:53.122
Haven't been stumped yet.

04:55.292 --> 04:58.160
Okay, I see what
your problem is.

04:58.195 --> 05:00.329
I-I-I tried to buy
a sweater online,

05:00.364 --> 05:02.198
and I-I think
I got a virus.

05:02.232 --> 05:04.600
No, the porn's
not the problem.

05:04.635 --> 05:06.102
Your browser history shows

05:06.136 --> 05:07.937
that you've been going
to kinkylatinas.net.

05:07.971 --> 05:10.206
But that site has
a bunch of malware.

05:10.240 --> 05:11.407
Oh.

05:11.441 --> 05:12.842
Personally, I'd recommend
College Latinas.

05:12.876 --> 05:15.678
I mean, I wanna see Latinas,
but I also want them to

05:15.712 --> 05:17.680
Speak English. speak English.
Yes, exactly.

05:17.714 --> 05:20.516
Wow. So you're into that kind
of stuff, too?

05:20.550 --> 05:22.385
Uh-huh.

05:23.854 --> 05:26.122
Would you, uh, would you have
dinner with me?

05:26.156 --> 05:27.890
Absolutely.

05:27.924 --> 05:30.359
Excuse me. I bought this
laptop here yesterday,

05:30.394 --> 05:33.229
but when I got home I noticed
the apple already had

05:33.263 --> 05:35.831
a bite taken out of it!

05:40.937 --> 05:42.571
So, yeah, I was
the first woman

05:42.606 --> 05:44.640
to ride her bike
cross-country with no seat.

05:44.675 --> 05:46.008
Gosh, that's neat, Sonja.

05:46.043 --> 05:47.376
And-and where'd
you go to college?

05:47.411 --> 05:49.478
I think Syracuse,
but I don't know.

05:49.513 --> 05:52.148
My face was buried
in a pillow all four years.

05:52.182 --> 05:54.550
Wow, sounds like you took
a full class load.

05:56.286 --> 05:59.388
Oh, Glenn, I'm so glad
you asked me out.

05:59.423 --> 06:00.990
Whenever I talk
about stuff like this,

06:01.024 --> 06:02.425
most people look at me

06:02.459 --> 06:04.160
like I'm some kind
of disgusting perv.

06:04.194 --> 06:05.394
Me, too, but who cares?

06:05.429 --> 06:07.263
You should never be afraid
to be different.

06:07.297 --> 06:08.264
Hoo.

06:08.298 --> 06:09.265
Hoo.

06:09.299 --> 06:11.767
Whom.

06:15.772 --> 06:17.039
Morning.

06:17.074 --> 06:19.875
Morning.

06:19.910 --> 06:22.078
We kind of had
a crazy night.

06:22.112 --> 06:23.512
Yeah, we... Did we?

06:23.547 --> 06:24.714
I don't really remember,

06:24.748 --> 06:27.483
but I do feel like I might
be down a couple of quarts.

06:28.719 --> 06:31.220
Well, even though you seemed
like a sure thing,

06:31.254 --> 06:33.923
I really wanted
to make sure.

06:35.459 --> 06:37.893
Oh, my God!
You roofied me?!

06:37.928 --> 06:39.095
Are you mad?

06:39.129 --> 06:42.732
No. I'm in love!

06:45.001 --> 06:46.202
Sonja, honey,
stay right here.

06:46.236 --> 06:48.070
I just have to go
to the bathroom.

06:48.105 --> 06:49.205
Wait, Glenn.

06:49.239 --> 06:52.241
Take this wine glass.
We can use it later.

06:52.275 --> 06:54.176
My God, I...

06:54.211 --> 06:56.045
I've never been so happy!

07:00.401 --> 07:03.136
I'm telling you guys,
Sonja is the perfect woman.

07:03.171 --> 07:05.739
She's every bit as kinky
and as insatiable as I am.

07:05.773 --> 07:06.340
Really?

07:06.365 --> 07:08.341
I thought you said she was
just some computer geek.

07:08.342 --> 07:09.609
She is.

07:09.644 --> 07:12.746
Her mouth has enough storage
space for a giggity-byte. Oh!

07:14.048 --> 07:16.049
Geez, you changed your
relationship status already?

07:16.084 --> 07:17.617
When you know, you know.

07:17.652 --> 07:19.419
All right, but just
be careful, ya know?

07:19.454 --> 07:21.021
You don't wanna rush an
important decision.

07:21.055 --> 07:22.422
I'll take
the cheeseburger meal.

07:22.457 --> 07:24.524
Would you like to make it
an extra large meal?

07:24.559 --> 07:27.094
Uh...

07:52.420 --> 07:53.920
N-No. Yes.

07:53.955 --> 07:55.088
No.

07:55.123 --> 07:57.424
You sure? It's only
29 cents more.

07:57.458 --> 07:58.658
Yes.

07:58.693 --> 08:00.427
No.

08:05.199 --> 08:06.833
What the hell?

08:09.670 --> 08:10.904
Stewie, what are you doing
up here?

08:10.938 --> 08:12.706
Brian!

08:12.740 --> 08:13.907
It's not what you think!

08:13.941 --> 08:15.876
All right, I came up here
for a photo shoot

08:15.910 --> 08:17.844
and it just got way,
way out of hand!

08:17.879 --> 08:18.979
You're having tea.

08:19.013 --> 08:20.514
How is that
out of hand?

08:20.548 --> 08:21.982
Is your shirt
on backwards?

08:22.016 --> 08:24.618
Please! You can't tell Rupert
I was up here, all right?

08:24.652 --> 08:26.319
He wouldn't understand.
He'll kill himself, Brian!

08:26.354 --> 08:27.754
He's been through so much
already!

08:27.789 --> 08:29.523
He can't take much more!

08:29.557 --> 08:31.725
Brian, he watched
his brother drown!

08:31.759 --> 08:32.959
Stewie, relax.

08:32.994 --> 08:34.928
You're getting all
worked up over nothing.

08:34.962 --> 08:36.563
Says the guy who freaks out

08:36.597 --> 08:38.565
every time
a fire engine goes by.

08:39.634 --> 08:41.601
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!
Oh, my God!

08:43.404 --> 08:46.740
Peter, Peter, you hear that?!

08:46.774 --> 08:50.877
I'm matching the sound!

08:50.912 --> 08:52.846
Is what I'm doing helping?

08:56.450 --> 08:58.785
Glenn, why did you
bring me here?

08:58.820 --> 09:00.020
Well, I've always had
this fantasy

09:00.054 --> 09:01.555
of having sex on
the basketball court

09:01.589 --> 09:03.056
in front of my
high school principal.

09:03.090 --> 09:07.227
Only problem is he's
now completely senile.

09:07.261 --> 09:09.763
Yeah, you like this,
Principal Goodrich, huh?

09:09.797 --> 09:10.997
Remember you once
suspended me

09:11.032 --> 09:12.532
for showing my wiener
in school?

09:12.567 --> 09:13.900
I did?

09:13.935 --> 09:16.269
This isn't as much fun
as I thought it would be.

09:16.304 --> 09:18.205
I'm sorry, Sonja,
I don't think I can finish.

09:18.239 --> 09:20.273
You never could finish,
Quagmire!

09:20.308 --> 09:22.375
Donahue, get in there!

09:23.945 --> 09:26.813
Okay, Glenn, now that we've
covered ourselves in black ink,

09:26.848 --> 09:28.448
let's do it until
we've created

09:28.482 --> 09:31.518
every character in
the Chinese alphabet.

09:41.262 --> 09:43.296
When all said and done,

09:43.331 --> 09:46.399
Quagmire body tell story
of sadness.

09:49.604 --> 09:52.138
Wow, I can't even imagine
what twisted deviant act

09:52.173 --> 09:53.773
you've thought of this time.

09:53.808 --> 09:56.343
I want you to have sex
with your father.

09:56.377 --> 09:57.844
What?!

09:57.879 --> 09:59.579
Yep, and I'm gonna watch.

09:59.614 --> 10:00.747
Hi, Glenn.

10:00.781 --> 10:02.816
Are you crazy?! No!
No way!

10:02.850 --> 10:05.418
Glenn, remember, the thing we love
most about each other

10:05.453 --> 10:07.087
is that we push
each other

10:07.121 --> 10:10.523
way beyond
our normal boundaries.

10:10.558 --> 10:12.859
Did you enjoy your stay
at the Marriott?

10:12.894 --> 10:14.694
No, I did not.

10:18.099 --> 10:21.534
Oh, well, excuse me for not
being six months old anymore!

10:21.569 --> 10:23.470
Oh, and here come
the tears!

10:23.504 --> 10:26.206
The show is starting,
everyone! Come on down!

10:27.775 --> 10:29.542
What's all that noise?

10:29.577 --> 10:31.044
What the hell's
going on up there?

10:31.078 --> 10:32.579
We're in a fight is
what's going on!

10:32.613 --> 10:34.681
Brian, I need you to settle
an argument for us:

10:34.715 --> 10:35.882
am I Hitler?

10:35.917 --> 10:37.384
Because I don't think
that I am,

10:37.418 --> 10:40.287
but maybe-maybe
I'm off base on this.

10:40.321 --> 10:41.421
Stewie, take it easy.

10:41.455 --> 10:42.455
No, you know what?

10:42.490 --> 10:43.890
You may as well call
your family now

10:43.891 --> 10:45.158
because I'm not going
to Sarasota.

10:45.192 --> 10:46.893
I don't care
if we can't get a refund,

10:46.928 --> 10:47.961
we're through!

10:47.995 --> 10:49.095
Here, Brian, you take him.

10:49.130 --> 10:50.363
Maybe you can make him happy.

10:50.398 --> 10:51.665
What?
You heard me. Take him.

10:51.699 --> 10:53.433
Do whatever you want
with him, I don't care.

10:53.467 --> 10:54.701
Rupert and I are over!

10:54.735 --> 10:55.769
Are you sure?

10:55.803 --> 10:56.870
Yes, we're done.

10:56.904 --> 10:58.338
I just hope we can
handle it better

10:58.372 --> 11:00.307
than blue and yellow
did when they split up.

11:00.341 --> 11:02.242
You were supposed to have
the kids here by 5:00.

11:02.276 --> 11:03.343
We have plans.

11:03.377 --> 11:04.477
It's 5:15.

11:04.512 --> 11:05.946
Stop busting my hump, Alicia.

11:05.980 --> 11:07.213
Okay, you know
what, let's not...

11:07.248 --> 11:08.715
let's not do this
in front of the kids.

11:08.749 --> 11:09.983
God, you're right.

11:10.017 --> 11:11.217
What ever happened to us?

11:11.252 --> 11:13.053
Hey, baby, you
ready for dinner?

11:13.087 --> 11:14.220
What's up, Scott?

11:14.255 --> 11:16.222
We gonna get
some barbecue.

11:19.427 --> 11:20.593
Hey, guys.

11:20.628 --> 11:22.362
No, indoors, not okay.
No, no, no, no, no, no.

11:22.396 --> 11:23.830
Don't do it.
Nighttime, not allowed.

11:23.864 --> 11:25.198
What? There's nothing
wrong with this.

11:25.232 --> 11:27.100
No, no way, give me those.

11:28.602 --> 11:29.703
Oh, my God.

11:29.737 --> 11:31.104
Quagmire,
what the hell happened?

11:31.138 --> 11:32.872
Is this another one
of those sex-related injuries

11:32.907 --> 11:34.040
you keep getting?

11:34.075 --> 11:35.375
Yeah, it seems like lately

11:35.409 --> 11:37.844
that girlfriend of yours is
taking things a little too far.

11:37.878 --> 11:39.946
No, she's not;
everything's great with us.

12:02.503 --> 12:04.371
Are you guys still talking
about Sonja?

12:04.405 --> 12:05.739
All right, I should
probably get going.

12:05.773 --> 12:06.973
Sonja and I are supposed to go

12:06.974 --> 12:09.642
to a "Brown Eyes
Wide Shut" party.

12:09.677 --> 12:11.678
Geez, I don't know what's
going on with him.

12:11.712 --> 12:13.747
But I guess love does
funny things to people.

12:13.781 --> 12:15.115
Look at Forrest Gump.

12:15.149 --> 12:16.383
Hi, Forrest.

12:16.417 --> 12:19.019
I know you just got back
from Vietnam and you love me,

12:19.053 --> 12:20.787
but I'm gonna go run a train

12:20.821 --> 12:22.789
with this group
of Black Panthers I just met.

12:22.823 --> 12:24.791
Okay, Jenny.

12:24.825 --> 12:26.126
Hi, Forrest.

12:26.160 --> 12:28.495
I know you came all this way
to New York to visit me,

12:28.529 --> 12:29.662
but I'm gonna go do blow

12:29.697 --> 12:31.498
and have sex
with a bunch of stockbrokers.

12:31.532 --> 12:33.466
Okay, Jenny.

12:33.501 --> 12:34.634
Hi, Forrest.

